v 3
d equaids: AIDS and QUAIDS demand systems for survey data - elasticities of the households, the individuals or the market, with analytic standard errors (robust, cluster, svy); missing prices and correction for the non-buyers
d
d Author: Abdelkrim Araar, Universite Laval / PEP
d Support: aabd@ecn.ulaval.ca
d Version : 1.2.0
d License : GPL-3.0-or-later
d
d Almost ideal demand system (Deaton and Muellbauer 1980) and its quadratic
d extension (Banks, Blundell and Lewbel 1997), demographics by Ray's scaling,
d estimated by iterated FGNLS (Gauss-Newton, analytic Jacobian, in Mata).
d Elasticities of the households (the mean of the household elasticities,
d the default), of the individuals (weights times household size), of the
d market (aggregate) and of a reference household (at the means), and the
d plain mean of the household elasticities, all with analytic standard errors
d from the exact influence function of the whole procedure, robust, by
d cluster or by survey design (svyset), or a bootstrap of the whole procedure. Missing prices of the non-buyers filled by
d group means (pimpute), correction for the non-buyers (Shonkwiler and Yen
d 1999, selection) with the probits in the standard errors.
d Diagnostics before estimation (equaidsdiag), estat diagnostics, Engel curves
d after estimation (estat engel), dialog box, examples of the help run from
d links (equaids_examples); example data installed (sysuse mexico_2014_cereals).
d
d Requires: Stata 14.2 or later
d
d Distribution-Date: 20260929
d
